@{
    Layout = null;
    var isAuthed = User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true;
}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Help — Candace Holder</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <script src="~/js/tailwind-config-app.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.0/css/all.min.css" />
    <style>
        html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
        .doc-section { scroll-margin-top: 80px; }
    </style>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/theme.css" asp-append-version="true" />
</head>
<body class="bg-slate-950 text-slate-50 font-sans antialiased">

<!-- ── Nav ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<header class="sticky top-0 z-50 bg-slate-950/90 backdrop-blur border-b border-slate-800/60 shadow-lg">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 flex items-center justify-between h-16">
        <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2.5 hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">
            <div class="w-8 h-8 brand-logo rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center shadow">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-address-book text-slate-50 text-sm"></i>
            </div>
            <span class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tight">Candace <span class="brand-text">Holder</span></span>
        </a>
        <a href="@(isAuthed ? "/" : "/Auth/Login")" class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-brand/10 text-brand border border-brand/30 text-xs font-semibold hover:bg-brand/20 transition-colors">
            @if (isAuthed) { <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left mr-1"></i><text>Back to App</text> }
            else { <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right-to-bracket mr-1"></i><text>Sign In</text> }
        </a>
    </div>
</header>

<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 space-y-12 text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">

    <section>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-slate-50 mb-3">How it works</h1>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Pick an area, save the addresses you want, then skip trace them to get the owner's name, phone, and email.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="find" class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50 mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass-location text-brand mr-2"></i>1. Find addresses</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">The <b class="text-slate-50">Search</b> page has two ways to choose a region:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li><b class="text-slate-50">Address Search → Radius</b> — enter an address and pick a radius (0.1–2 miles). Every address within that circle is listed, closest first.</li>
            <li><b class="text-slate-50">Address Search → Single Address</b> — just that one property.</li>
            <li><b class="text-slate-50">Draw on Map</b> — jump to a city or ZIP, click <b class="text-slate-50">Select Area</b>, then click and drag a box. Every address inside the box is listed. Keep boxes under about 5 miles across.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">Addresses come from OpenStreetMap, with a Google Maps fallback in newer neighborhoods OpenStreetMap hasn't mapped yet. A single search returns up to 150 addresses.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="save" class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50 mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-bookmark text-brand mr-2"></i>2. Save the ones you want</h2>
        <p>Tick the addresses in the results list (or <b class="text-slate-50">Select All</b>), then <b class="text-slate-50">Save Selected</b>. Use the filter box to narrow by street name. <b class="text-slate-50">Export CSV</b> downloads the list without saving anything.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="trace" class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50 mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass-dollar text-brand mr-2"></i>3. Skip trace</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">On <b class="text-slate-50">Saved Leads</b>, click the <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass-dollar text-orange-600"></i> button on a row, or tick several rows and use <b class="text-slate-50">Skip Trace</b> in the toolbar (up to 100 at a time).</p>
        <p class="mb-3">Each lookup goes to BatchData, which returns the owner's name, their phone numbers (mobile first) and email addresses. You're only charged when it finds a match.</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li><span class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-red-100 text-red-700 text-xs font-bold">DNC</span> marks a number on a Do Not Call list — don't cold call or text it.</li>
            <li><span class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-red-100 text-red-700 text-xs font-bold">Litigator</span> marks a person known for suing over calls and texts — don't contact them.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/10 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-amber-700">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-dollar-sign mr-1.5"></i>
            Every matched skip trace is billed by BatchData. Only owners and managers can run skip traces.
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="work" class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50 mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-list-check text-brand mr-2"></i>4. Work your leads</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Set each lead's status: New → Contacted → Appt Set → Won / Lost. Won and Lost leads move to the <b class="text-slate-50">Closed</b> tab.</li>
            <li>Click the <i class="fa-solid fa-pen"></i> pencil to correct owner info by hand, or <i class="fa-solid fa-note-sticky"></i> to add notes.</li>
            <li>Open a lead for its map, every contact found, and its history.</li>
            <li>Archived leads can be restored from the <b class="text-slate-50">Archived</b> tab.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="compliance" class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50 mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved text-brand mr-2"></i>Before you call or text</h2>
        <p>BatchData flags Do Not Call numbers and known litigators, and leaves out numbers with TCPA restrictions. Still follow TCPA rules for texts and autodialed calls, and honor any opt-out request right away.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="team" class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50 mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-users text-brand mr-2"></i>Adding people</h2>
        <p>Public sign-up is turned off. Invite people from <b class="text-slate-50">Team</b> in the account menu. Owners and managers can skip trace; reps can view and work leads but can't run paid lookups.</p>
    </section>
</main>

<footer class="border-t border-slate-800/60">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
        Candace Holder &copy; 2026
    </div>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
